course: dictionary
lesson: 14991
title: Reprimand: a formal telling-off
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words sound stiff and grown-up. Reprimand is one of them. To reprimand someone means to tell them off officially for doing something wrong. «The head teacher reprimanded Sam for running in the corridor.»
explain: Read the clues. Sam ran in the corridor, which was wrong, and the head teacher spoke to him about it. So reprimanded must mean told off. Check by swapping in your meaning: «The head teacher told Sam off for running in the corridor» still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Reprimand can also be a noun, a thing you get. «The worker received a reprimand for being late every day.» Here a reprimand is the formal telling-off itself. Phrases to listen for: «a stern reprimand» and «be reprimanded for». In everyday talk, you might say «tell off», «get told off» or «get into trouble».
fact: To reprimand someone means to tell them off formally for doing something wrong.
fact: Reprimand can be a verb (you reprimand someone) or a noun (you get a reprimand).
fact: «A stern reprimand» means a strict, serious telling-off.
fact: Reprimands are often given in schools and at work.
fact: Everyday words for reprimand include «tell off» and «get into trouble».
exercise: «The teacher reprimanded Tom for talking during the test.» What does reprimanded mean? | Forgot all about him | Praised him loudly | Gave him a prize | *Told him off formally
exercise: Mum says, «Dad got a reprimand at work for being late.» What is a reprimand here? | A new job | *A formal telling-off | A party with cake | A holiday
exercise: «The manager gave her a stern reprimand.» What does stern reprimand mean? | A long walk home | A quick hug | *A strict, serious telling-off | A happy song
test: «The head teacher reprimanded the boys for fighting.» Which phrase means the same as reprimanded? | *Told them off | Gave them sweets | Asked them to sing | Sent them to the library
test: In which sentence is reprimand a noun, a thing someone gets? | Mia reprimands her friend every day. | Mia will reprimand her friend today. | *Mia got a reprimand for being rude.
exam: «She was reprimanded for being late, and it was a stern reprimand.» What does reprimanded mean? | Moved to a new class | *Told off formally for doing wrong | Asked to sit down quietly | Given a medal for being early
